      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T00:00:00Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the exploit and Curve-creation traces, verified Curve source, official post-mortem, commit-pinned reproduction, pre-exploit runtime, and reported loss. The exploit calls flash directly on 0x46161158b1947d9149e066d6d31af1283b2d377c; verified source shows flash omits the nonReentrant modifier used by the other state-changing entry points. The vulnerable check is in the Curve runtime itself, not in its delegated liquidity libraries. The Curve hash is 0xf37f24c57a627b1e196d7f971a4fadcc974b17333f82db976e6cb50da774e5b2 at creation and immediately before exploitation, and its runtime contains no SELFDESTRUCT, so deployment is the latest code change."
